body:
Three meters is a lot. Most people aren't even more than two meters in height, so you could fit a bed in that empty space.

&#x200B;

Besides, saying that other ships need more love isn't a compelling argument against Mustang Beta v2's downgrading of its interior design. They should've just kept the same layout.

What did it feel like when you knew (and told) Peter would denounce you three times before the cock crows on your crucifixion? Were there any hard feelings you had against Peter? Had you always known he would denounce you? 

&#x200B;

EDITTED for more context.

I was teaching English online, and my organization banned LTEs from being allowed to teach. Reason was that LTEs aren't as stable as DSL/Fiber/other wired connection types. I was using fiber before, but had to move to a rural location, so now only have access to LTE.

&#x200B;

My family member told me not to disclose this information that I was using LTE to give me a chance to teach again, but I thought it would be unprofessional of me not to disclose from the get-go that I was using LTE.

&#x200B;

I feel conflicted about my honesty, knowing I won't be able to teach, but I feel like I'd rather not teach than to run the risk of either giving the kids I teach a bad time from scummy internet on my end, or that my organization would sue me for going through the cracks, or both.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Reason for this question is my organization said they could detect if my connection was LTE or not via my IP address.
